      "writtenOn": "2018-12-20T19:17:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this the only possible result?\nI think it depends on the exact timing, and there are at least these 3 possible results (all of which you have seen):\n  (a) master receives a NAK for a byte it sent to Cr50; this happens ifCr50 resets i2c bus \u003d\u003e sets SDA\u003d0 while AP sends a 0, so AP doesn\u0027t see it until it checks for NAK.\n  (a) master sees a bus arbitration error if it tries to send a 1 while Cr50 is resetting i2c (ie Cr50 writes SDA\u003d0 overridding master\u0027s write of SDA\u003d1).\n  (b) master sees no bus error, but never receives IRQ, if poller aborts transaction after physical i2c bus transaction was completed successfully.",
